From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Haoze <haozegao0602@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 08:57:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 02/10] [G3.1] power capture only with GVSOC_POWER_CAPTURE=1
 (owner-approved gate; did not stop the memory growth)

Symptom: tests/gvsoc/run.py gemm with K-tile 256 (256x256x256:256,256,256, 256x768x256:...)
grows the simulator to the 13 GB cap in 30-50 s. TimeEngine::init now calls start_capture
only if env GVSOC_POWER_CAPTURE=1; power_capture_advance already returns early when capture
was not started. This removes the failing make ice_power system() call, but it is NOT the
cause of the growth: with it (and with pwr_interval_ps=9e15) run rung1a-gemm256 was still
killed at the cap (LOG experiments/smolvla-e2e-baseline/LOG.md, G3.1 follow-up). The change
lives in soft_hier/gvsoc_core.patch (hunk for engine/src/time/time_engine.cpp) and is applied
to the core working tree.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 soft_hier/gvsoc_core.patch | 24 +++++++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

